  "_README": [
    "slug -> the dish's actual name, for the index card only. The note's own `title` is",
    "untouched and is what the detail page shows underneath the dish name, so nothing is",
    "lost — this file only decides what the front page says.",
    "",
    "Why a curated map and not a regex: the raw titles are Paprika/YouTube captures, and",
    "the cruft is not mechanical. 'The BEST Garbanzo Bean Stew of Your Life | Spanish",
    "Potaje De Garbanzos' -> 'Potaje de Garbanzos' and 'Phillips make a red pepper tomato",
    "soup' -> 'Red Pepper Tomato Soup' are judgement calls no pattern gets right.",
    "",
    "Why here and not in the note frontmatter, which is otherwise the source of truth:",
    "these notes are a Paprika export and a re-export would drop an added key. A missing",
    "entry here just falls back to the raw title, so drift shows as a loud title on the",
    "grid rather than as wrong data. `python3 -m recipes.dish_check` lists stale keys.",
    "",
    "Only slugs whose dish name differs from the raw title appear. Edited by hand; the",
    "Hub loads it once at import, so restart :5002 after editing."
  ],

